7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]still-eligible runs into a restorable trash in the background. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Protections are re-verified before every move and again before any [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]permanent purge.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]actionable_run_prune_notifications.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/actionable_run_prune_notifications.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1rd[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1rd/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust run-trash contract in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_quarantine[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_quarantine: add a sase-core module that quarantines confirmed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ACE-run dirs into a journaled, restorable trash by atomic rename, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-checking every protection first. It also lists, restores, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]protection-verifies purges, with PyO3 bindings and tests. The unattended[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]apply refusal stays.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python facade, review snapshots, and CLI apply/restore[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]trash_callers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_quarantine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]trash_callers: ratchet the core pin, add the Python facade and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]review-snapshot payload module, make `prune-runs --apply` quarantine [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fresh-intersect-reviewed runs, and post a result notification. `artifact[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trash` gains run batches, and the artifact index stays consistent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hourly preview emits an actionable, beautiful notification[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]preview_notification[dim] · [dim][/dim]after trash_callers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview_notification: the chop purges expired batches, writes a review [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot, and attaches the review payload. It redesigns the report with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project display names and per-project rows, supersedes stale previews, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and drops the \"preview-only\" copy.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI prune review modal behind notification Enter[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]review_modal[dim] · [dim][/dim]after trash_callers, preview_notification[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]review_modal: route Enter on payload-bearing report notifications to a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new prune review modal with ready, blocked, missing, and running states.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]On confirm it submits the CLI apply as a durable proc and reports [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]completion. Includes badges, footer, help, visual snapshots, and an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]end-to-end fixture test.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1rd","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1rd.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-bd7a693ae8ec0c40675c610f871e2234","started_at":"2026-11-05T11:23:12.478883+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rd","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rd.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rd.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rd.3",